## G. root cause per storage check (from F + the code of 457a0c1)
insert_task / insert_event: the row carries tenant_id -> PostgREST 400 (column does not exist) -> FAIL (correct).
get_task / get_tasks / get_events: the filter tenant_id=eq.<run tenant> -> 400 -> FAIL (correct).
cleanup: DELETE …?tenant_id=eq.<run tenant> -> 400 -> "cleanup failed" (correct: it cannot prove the run left nothing; F proves it).
update_task: PATCH tasks?task_id=eq.<random run id> sends no tenant_id; it matched 0 rows and PostgREST answered 204 —
  supabase_store.update_task accepted (200, 204) alone, so the check printed [ok] although NOTHING was updated -> a false "ok".
  It was also the only check that made `connected=True` for storage (definition: a write accepted or a row read back).
  -> fixed in this batch (R-161c, log 127).
"other tenant cannot read the row" [ok]: true without any server (documented in R-161); it does not show the store worked.

